--
N5008 [temp.constr.decl]/3 + [temp.constr.atomic]/1: the requires-clause of a
function template (and of a member template of a class template
specialization) is checked under the parameter mapping of the constrained
declaration.  Guards the template-map based check: concept-ids over a
parameter pack (`all_small<Args...>`, `first_is<T, Args...>`, a non-type
argument with a pack `arity<3, Args...>`), a class parameter named from a
member's clause through the class's own specialization
(`typename box<T>::value_type`), each against an unconstrained twin so the
constrained one must win exactly when satisfied.  Non-vacuous: the last
assertion states a wrong value and must FAIL.
